  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The present in -ere",
   "texto": [
    "**-ere** verbs use the following endings: **io -o**, **tu -i**, **lui/lei/Lei -e**, **noi -iamo**, **voi -ete**, **loro -ono**.",
    "Attention to differences with -are: the third person singular ends in **-e** (**lui prende**, **lei scrive**; no * -a *). The second plural ends in **-ete** (**voi prendete**). And in the third plural it ends in **-ono**, with an emphasis on the root: **PREN-do-no**, **SCRÍ-vo-no**, **VÉ-do-no**."
   ]
  },
